# Rigor core overlay — supplemental core signatures.
#
# --- BigDecimal precision readers (issue #2969) ---
#
# rbs 4.2 ships `stdlib/bigdecimal/0/big_decimal.rbs` without `precision`, `scale`,
# `precision_scale` or `n_significant_digits`, and the bigdecimal gem's own `sig/` (4.1.3)
# omits them too, so `BigDecimal("1.5").precision` reported `call.undefined-method` on correct code.
#
# Upstream: bigdecimal 4.1.3 `ext/bigdecimal/bigdecimal.c` registers the four readers as instance
# methods (`rb_define_method(rb_cBigDecimal, "precision", ...)`, and likewise for the other three).
# Their documented results: `precision -> integer` (decimal digits), `scale -> integer`,
# `precision_scale -> [integer, integer]`, and `n_significant_digits -> integer`.
#
# bigdecimal is a bundled gem, not a default library, so this file is gated on it
# (`Rigor::Environment::RbsLoader::LIBRARY_SUPPLEMENT_CORE_OVERLAYS`). Without the library the file would
# open a phantom `BigDecimal` that nothing else declares.
#
# The methods sit on a module the class includes, not as direct `def`s, so a later rbs or a project
# `sig/` that declares one of them directly overrides it instead of raising
# `DuplicatedMethodDefinitionError` (the same shape as `process.rbs` and `ruby41_core_overlay`).

module RigorCoreOverlay
  module BigDecimalPrecision
    def precision: () -> Integer
    def scale: () -> Integer
    def precision_scale: () -> [Integer, Integer]
    def n_significant_digits: () -> Integer
  end
end

class BigDecimal
  include RigorCoreOverlay::BigDecimalPrecision
end
